 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "`ZeroOneForm/Basic.lean:211` defines `zeroOneSobolevSections`, and `:279` has only `instance zeroOneSobolevSections.instCompleteSpace`. A grep for normed instances under `Sobolev/` finds only the two private ones in Annihilator.lean:271,278. The PR description says: 'The public statement cannot use private instances.'",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/VectorBundle/Sobolev/CauchyRiemann/Annihilator.lean",
   "fix": "Move both instances, public, to `ZeroOneForm/Basic.lean` next to `zeroOneSobolevSections.instCompleteSpace` and delete the private copies. Then restate the theorem as `(eLpNorm \u03b8 q (volume.restrict Q')).toReal \u2264 C * \u2016\u039b\u2016`, dropping the `K` binder and its hypothesis.",
   "issue": "`instNormedAddCommGroupZeroOneSobolevSections` and `instNormedSpaceZeroOneSobolevSections` (line 278) are general instances on the public type `zeroOneSobolevSections`, hidden as `private` here. Because they are private, the public `exists_eLpNorm_le_of_forall_eq_setIntegral` cannot state its bound with `\u2016\u039b\u2016` and takes `\u2200 K, (\u2200 w, \u2016\u039b w\u2016 \u2264 K * \u2016w\u2016) \u2192 \u2026 \u2264 C * K` instead, so downstream users (the next Fredholm step) must restate the operator-norm bound or redeclare the instances.",
   "line": 271
  }
 ],
